{
  "requirement": "Distinguishes a domain operation failure, a missing agent, a provider connection or request failure, an agent protocol failure, and an error encoding or decoding the output.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub enum ValidationError<E> {\n    Graph(E),\n    NoAgentConfigured,\n    Agent(String),\n    Provider(std::io::Error),\n    Output(serde_json::Error),\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<E: Debug> Debug for ValidationError<E>;\nimpl<E: Display> Display for ValidationError<E>;\nimpl<E: Error + 'static> Error for ValidationError<E>;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement fixes the five-variant enum `ValidationError<E>` and requires that each variant distinguish one kind of failure. It also names `Debug`, `Display` and `Error` implementations, but it doesn't specify any message text or `source` behavior. I judged the tests against the five variants and the trait implementations.\n\nI did not request implementation source. The expected behavior comes from the requirement text.\n\n**Variant coverage**\n- **`Graph(E)`**:\n  - `tests/contracts.rs#fn[refresh_propagates_load_decode_check_execution_and_save_errors]` injects domain failures at the load, read, edges, execute and store stages.\n  - It asserts each one surfaces as `ValidationError::Graph(actual)` with the matching stage string.\n  - It also checks that the saved record is unchanged and that the execution and write counts are as expected.\n  - `graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[agent_errors_expose_the_agreed_string_payload]` checks that a `Graph` error's `source()` is the inner error.\n- **`NoAgentConfigured`**:\n  - `graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls]` verifies without an agent.\n  - It asserts `Err(NoAgentConfigured)`.\n  - It also asserts that no record is stored and nothing is read.\n- **`Agent(String)`**:\n  - `graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[invalid_typed_submission_is_an_agent_error]` asserts `Agent(_)` for an invalid typed submission through both `ask` and `verify_with_agent`.\n  - `agent/tests.rs#fn[assistant_text_and_provider_failure_cannot_become_typed_results]` asserts `Agent` for a text-only assistant, and the error message contains the expected text.\n  - `agent_errors_expose_the_agreed_string_payload` asserts the payload is a `String`, the `Display` output is \"agent: provider detail\", and `source()` is `None`.\n- **`Provider(io::Error)`**:\n  - `assistant_text_and_provider_failure_cannot_become_typed_results` asserts `Provider` for a permanent provider failure and checks its message.\n  - `agent/configured.rs#fn[configured_agents_initialize_only_when_asked_and_report_setup_errors]` asserts `Provider` for a missing credential, and the `Display` output names the environment variable.\n- **`Output(serde_json::Error)`**:\n  - The \"decode\", \"stale decode\" and \"unversioned decode\" stages of `refresh_propagates_load_decode_check_execution_and_save_errors` assert `Output`.\n  - `refresh_serialization_failure_preserves_the_saved_record` and `serialization_failure_leaves_the_existing_record_unchanged` assert `Output` for an encode failure.\n  - The second of those also checks the `Display` text and that the stored record is unchanged.\n\n**Trait implementations**\n- The `Debug`, `Display` and `Error` implementations are exercised.\n  - `Display` is asserted for the `Agent`, `Provider` and `Output` variants.\n  - `Error::source` is asserted for `Agent` (`None`) and `Graph` (the inner error).\n  - `Debug` is used in the panic formatting of the refresh test.\n  - The bounds and trait implementations are also checked at compile time, because the public API and test code use them.\n- `Display` text for `Graph` and `NoAgentConfigured`, and `source` for `Provider` and `Output`, are not asserted. The requirement specifies none of that behavior, so I don't count it as a gap.\n\nNo requirement-violating behavior stands out that these tests would accept. In particular, mixing up variants would fail the matches in these tests. `tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` only supports the exported surface and isn't needed for the judgment.",
  "references": "48bed995c1f03f710524a5445fe98cfa696792ed02ff389a810818fa5239670c",
